\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{From trivial links to a connection}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The spin grading considered here anticommutes with a Clifford generator.
That generator exchanges its two grading spaces, so the grading has trace zero.
For this grading and a graded-hermitian kernel #{K} with #{\Gamma K} invertible,
\ref{fdip-014D} then gives the graded index of its overlap operator as half the number of negative
eigenvalues of #{\Gamma K} minus half the number of positive ones. At trivial
links the two counts agree on every Wilson block by \ref{fdip-014F}.
Which other connections keep this index, and which integers can be read
from the links themselves?}
